.superpowers/

# AI-authored design specs — superseded by the code, stale within days
docs/superpowers/

# Private app modules. They live in a separate repository, cloned into noop/ by whoever
# has access; settings.gradle.kts loads noop/settings.gradle.kts when present, so this
# repo builds identically with or without the clone. Deliberately not a submodule: that
# would commit the private repo's URL here, which is the one thing this arrangement avoids.
noop/

# Generated score assets: deny by default, ship by exception.
# `:features:pulsar:importScore` writes every score it can build into this folder,
# including the multi-part exports that only a score-playing host can select (~3.8MB
# with no picker in this app). Listing them individually meant each new one had to be
# remembered; the folder rule means a regenerated score is ignored unless someone
# deliberately un-ignores it, which is the right way round for bytes that ship publicly.
# Note the `/*` — excluding the directory itself would make the negation below impossible.
features/pulsar/src/commonMain/composeResources/files/scores/*
!features/pulsar/src/commonMain/composeResources/files/scores/fifth-lead.json
